:: Different Approach [event main_quest] {"position":"3150,375","size":"100,100"}
I head down the hall toward $sister.callName's room. Her window is cracked open, and the warm air keeps nudging the curtains so the whole room seems to breathe. I leave the prototype on my desk this time. I've hit a wall with clients, and if anyone can help me think straight without a little push, it's her.

I knock twice. She answers before my hand is even back at my side.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
  { who: $sister,  text: "It's open!" },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

She's sprawled across her bed with her phone held up over her face and her feet propped against the wall. When she sees it's me, she lowers the phone onto her chest, but she doesn't bother sitting up.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
  { who: $player,  text: "Got a minute?" },
  { who: $sister,  text: "For you? I can probably spare four. What's up?" },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

I sit down on the corner of her bed and leave enough room between us that it doesn't feel like an ambush.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
  { who: $player,  text: "I hate to say it, but I need your help again." },
  { who: $sister,  text: "Again? I'm already doing your dishes, $player.name. What's next, you want me to do your taxes too?" },
  { who: $player,  text: "I know, I know. This is different, I promise. I don't need your time, I need your brain." },
  { who: $sister,  text: "Now I'm actually worried. You only say nice things about my brain when something's on fire. What happened?" },
  { who: $player,  text: "I spent the whole day emailing and calling people about the prototype, cafés and gyms and a tutoring center, and I got nothing. Everyone wants references, and nobody wants to be the first one to give me a chance to get any." },
  { who: $sister,  text: "Wait, back up. What does it actually do? $mom.callName says it 'reads rooms', which sounds like something a horoscope app would promise you." },
  { text: "I give her the version I give everyone, or I try to. It comes out a lot messier than it does in my emails." },
  { who: $player,  text: "Okay, so, you know how you walk into a place and you can tell in about two seconds whether you want to stay? It picks up on that stuff. How loud it is, how people are sitting, whether everybody's staring at their phones. And then it nudges the room a little so people relax, and relaxed people order another coffee and maybe a muffin. That's the idea, anyway. It sounds better when I have slides." },
  { who: $sister,  text: "No, it actually sounds kind of smart. A little creepy, but smart." },
  { who: $player,  text: "Thanks. I think." },
  { who: $sister,  text: "So everybody thinks it's cool, and nobody wants to be the guinea pig." },
  { who: $player,  text: "Pretty much." },
  { who: $sister,  text: "Then you need a guinea pig who already likes you, or at least one who's stuck with you." },
  { text: "She rolls onto her side and props her head on her hand, suddenly wide awake." },
  { who: $sister,  text: "Your diner. You're there five days a week anyway. Go talk to your manager and offer to test it during your own shifts, for free, and if it works, he gives you a quote or whatever it is you need." },
  { who: $player,  text: "$manager.callName? He laughs at me every time I mention the company." },
  { who: $sister,  text: "Then give him a reason to stop laughing. Put a couple of things on the menu that make him good money and see whether people order them more often with your gadget running. If they do, you've got your numbers." },
  { text: "I open my mouth to argue and realize I don't have anything." },
  { who: $player,  text: "That's actually really good. Why didn't I think of that?" },
  { who: $sister,  text: "Because you've been staring at the same screen for a week and forgot that other people exist. Keep it small, it costs him nothing and you do all the work. People tend to say yes when saying no is more effort." },
  { who: $player,  text: "And if he still says no?" },
  { text: "If he still says no, the prototype fits in my apron pocket just fine. I keep that part to myself." },
  { who: $sister,  text: "Then you ask him again, nicely, like a normal person. And text me after, I want to know whether we're celebrating or coming up with a plan B." },
  { who: $player,  text: "Deal. Thanks, $sister.callName, seriously. You might actually be a genius." },
  { who: $sister,  text: "I've been telling you that for years. It's nice that you're finally catching up." }
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

By the time I'm back in my room I already have a one-pager open and half a test plan for $diner.name typed out. My head is buzzing for a good reason, for once. Tomorrow I'll try again, and this time I'll have something to show.
<<NextQuest $player>>
